{"assets":["/statement-assets/ef53ed3a4e58e84dbde96b43ccfed9f9764e6b21a9a6985503a35c9a59d5db93.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"232","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Doe Graphs"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"John Doe decided that some mathematical object must be named after him. So he invented the Doe graphs. The Doe graphs are a family of undirected graphs, each of them is characterized by a single non-negative number — its order. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We'll denote a graph of order "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(k)"},{"kind":"text","text":", and we'll denote the number of vertices in the graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(k)"},{"kind":"text","text":" as "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(k)|"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then let's define the Doe graphs as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(0)"},{"kind":"text","text":" consists of a single vertex, that has number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" consists of two vertices with numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", connected by an edge. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n ≥ 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" is obtained from graphs "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" are joined in one graph, at that numbers of all vertices of graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" increase by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(n - 1)|"},{"kind":"text","text":" (for example, vertex number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" of graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n - 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" becomes vertex number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 + |D(n - 1)|"},{"kind":"text","text":"). After that two edges are added to the graph: the first one goes between vertices with numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(n - 1)|"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(n - 1)| + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", the second one goes between vertices with numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(n - 1)| + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that the definition of graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" implies, that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a connected graph, its vertices are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"|D(n)|"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ef53ed3a4e58e84dbde96b43ccfed9f9764e6b21a9a6985503a35c9a59d5db93.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The picture shows the Doe graphs of order 1, 2, 3 and 4, from left to right."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"John thinks that Doe graphs are that great because for them exists a polynomial algorithm for the search of Hamiltonian path. However, your task is to answer queries of finding the shortest-length path between the vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the graph "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"D(n)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A path between a pair of vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the graph is a sequence of vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"..."},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xk"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(k > 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" such, that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1 = u"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xk = v"},{"kind":"text","text":", and for any "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i < k)"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" are connected by a graph edge. The length of path "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"..."},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xk"},{"kind":"text","text":" is number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(k - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ t ≤ 105; 1 ≤ n ≤ 103"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of queries and the order of the given graph. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"t"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai, bi ≤ 1016"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai ≠ bi"},{"kind":"text","text":") — numbers of two vertices in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th query. It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai, bi ≤ |D(n)|"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please, do not use the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%lld"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specifier to read or write 64-bit integers in С++. It is preferred to use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cin"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" streams or the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"%I64d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" specifier. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query print a single integer on a single line — the length of the shortest path between vertices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bi"},{"kind":"text","text":". Print the answers to the queries in the order, in which the queries are given in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 5\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n1 5\n2 3\n2 4\n2 5\n3 4\n3 5\n4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1\n1\n2\n1\n2\n3\n1\n2\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"232C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/232/problem/C"}